Reason:
This loop adds a class to the active list when it changes from strict to DRR and has packets. However, if the class was already on the active list because it was previously a DRR and then changed to strict without removal, the list_add_tail causes a duplicate entry, leading to list corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
for (i = q->nstrict; i < nstrict; i++) {
    if (cl_is_active(&q->classes[i]))
        list_del_init(&q->classes[i].alist);
}
Reason:
This loop removes any class that is being changed from DRR to strict from the active list, ensuring that when the class is later changed back to DRR, it can be safely added again without duplication.

